  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=\\frac{5}{9x+18}-4\\,?$\n\nThe domain is\n$x\\in (-\\infty ,$\n{{field-1}}$)\\cup (${{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$).$",
  "worked_solution": "A reciprocal function is defined for all values of $x$ except those that make the denominator zero. So, to find the domain, we must exclude all values of $x$ that make the denominator zero.\n\nSetting the denominator equal to zero and solving, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x+18 & =0 \\\\ 9x & =-18 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{18}{9} \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (-2,\\infty ).$",
